their perfection is innate, consisting mostly of ease and without exertion;
in them there is no misfortune, nor higher, lower, and middle ranks.

Herons together with cranes ascend the supreme trees,
and crows also build nests, O bull among sages;
and these crows sleep, languid under the burden of their wombs in this season.

